~ start

???: Anunsyo sa lahat ng residente ng Zone 4! Mandatong pag-evacuate!
???: Pack your critical documents and move to the central public elementary school or our concrete barangay hall right now! 
???: A storm surge is headed straight for us! Get out of your houses!

PILI: Ernesto... 
PILI: That's your sister Mercy outside with the megaphone.

MERCY: Susmariosep... Pili! Ernesto! Why are you still hanging up birthday decorations?
MERCY: Look at these children! Why aren't they packed yet? Noni, put that crayon away, anak. Go find your slippers right now.

ERNESTO: Mercy, sit down first. You’ve been running around the barangay since dawn. 
ERNESTO: Those city officials always throw around those heavy English terms like 'storm surge' just to make people panic. They're 
ERNESTO: It's just a regular high-tide flood and some strong wind. We've survived five typhoons already this year alone, haven't we?

MERCY: The Mayor called all 138 of us barangay captains into an emergency meeting, Ernesto! This isn't something ordinary! 
MERCY: I don't know what a 'storm surge' means either but the coast guard already forced the fishermen to drag their boats straight up onto the national highway! The concrete elementary school classrooms are the only safe structures to block these winds! 
MERCY: We are doing a final door-to-door sweep so pack your bags and let Andrei help you load the children into the municipal truck!

ERNESTO: I am NOT moving my family to a crowded school building near the coast, Mercy.
ERNESTO: Our family has lived in Taklub for three generations.
ERNESTO: If I abandon this house tonight, who is going to watch over our copra beds?!
ERNESTO: Three months of my blood and sweat will turn to garbage in a single hour!
ERNESTO: ...
ERNESTO: The Millgate deal is our only chance to pay off what we owe this year. It's the only way I can buy school supplies for next term and feed these kids.
ERNESTO: I am not throwing our entire life away because they scared you! 
ERNESTO: We are staying. 
ERNESTO: Right HERE.

MERCY: Pride won't keep the ocean out of your floor, brother! 
MERCY: Every single family down this lane is giving me the exact same excuse about protecting their properties! 
MERCY: I am trying to save your lives, Ernesto, damn it!
MERCY: Pili, for the love of God, look at your babies! Look at Kiki! Tell him!

PILI: ...
PILI: Mercy...
PILI: Ernesto is right. The old trees have always kept us safe before. 
PILI: God wouldn't give our family this big blessing just to take it away right before our boy's eighth birthday.

MERCY: You two are going to drive me crazy... 
MERCY: Andrei, check on the kids. We have to finish checking the rest of the zone before midnight.

ANDREI: Hey, chief. Turning eight tomorrow?
ANDREI: Wow, you're almost taller than your Kuya Dodong now. Don't worry about your Tatay and my mom yelling. They’re just acting like regular old parents. 
ANDREI: ...
ANDREI: But listen to me carefully, okay?
ANDREI: My mom honestly believes the concrete school will keep everyone safe from the wind but the river is right behind those classrooms. 
ANDREI: If the wind gets too loud tonight and you see water creeping over these wooden floorboards, do not hide under the beds. 
ANDREI: You grab your baby sister Kiki immediately. Don't worry about your toys. You stay right next to your Ate Valerie and Kuya Dodong. 
ANDREI: Can you do that for me, Ollie?


- I understand, Kuya. I’ll keep Kiki safe.
	OLLIE: Okay. I’ll keep Kiki safe and hold onto Ate Valerie's hand if the water comes inside.
	ANDREI: That’s my boy. A real nurse's assistant. Valerie, keep the flashlights close to the door.
	VALERIE: We’ll stay together, Kuya Andrei. I won't let go of them.
	I don't know who is telling the truth anymore but my chest feels very heavy... and so, so cold.


- But Tatay said our coconut trees will keep us all safe.
	OLLIE: Tatay said they're like strong umbrellas. He said the rain can't even touch us here.
	ANDREI: Your Tatay loves those trees, Ollie, but even the strongest umbrellas can tear when the storm is too big. 
	ANDREI: Just... promise me you’ll be safe. Be ready to move if your Ate tells you to. You too, Dodong, Noni and Kiki. Don't hesitate. Just run.
	VALERIE: We’ll be ready, Kuya Andrei. I’ll hold onto them. 
	DODONG: I’ll carry Kiki, Kuya. I won't let go of her.
	NONI: Okay, Kuya Andrei... I’ll keep my shoes on.
	I don't know who is telling the truth, but my chest feels very heavy... and so, so cold.


MERCY: We have to go. We’ll pray for you tonight, Ernesto. 
MERCY: I hope to God you are right about those trees. If things get bad, get to the roof. Do you hear me? The roof!

ERNESTO: We'll be fine. Tell the barangay council we are secure here.

PILI: ...

